dren":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Surface tab index; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"keyboard: false"},{"type":"text","value":" forces "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"-1"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"idPrefix"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Generated"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Prefix for renderer-owned document IDs"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartSvgRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChartSvg"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scene-to-SVG renderer"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureText"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTextMeasurer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host measurer"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guide text measurement"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFocusChange"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(point: ChartPoint | null) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Primary focus callback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFocusGroupChange"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(points: readonly ChartPoint[]) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grouped focus callback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onSelect"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(point: ChartPoint | null) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pointer or keyboard activation callback"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onRender"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(context: ChartRenderContext) => void"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default SVG, complete surface, container, and scene after rendering"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"class"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra class on the inner "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inner host declarations applied after adapter sizing"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"className"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"None"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extra class on the rendered chart surface"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Callbacks are functions inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":", not Angular outputs. Replace the\ncomplete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" value when chart state changes so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OnPush"},{"type":"text","value":" change detection\ndelivers an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ngOnChanges"},{"type":"text","value":" update."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-template","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body template"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project a typed tooltip template into the chart:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<tanstack-chart [options]=\"chartOptions\">\n  <ng-template [tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"chartOptions.definition\" let-tooltip>\n    <ng-container [ngTemplateOutlet]=\"tooltip.defaultBody\" />\n    <series-detail [points]=\"tooltip.points\" />\n    @if (tooltip.pinned) {\n    <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"tooltip.dismiss()\">Close</button>\n    }\n  </ng-template>\n</tanstack-chart>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyDirective"},{"type":"text","value":" and Angular's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NgTemplateOutlet"},{"type":"text","value":" beside\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":". The context exposes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"points"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pinned"},{"type":"text","value":", and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dismiss"},{"type":"text","value":"; named template bindings are also available. Binding the same\ndefinition gives Angular's strict template checker the datum and x/y value\ntypes. Ordering, anchoring, placement, portaling, and pinning remain in the\ndefinition."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"exported-types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exported types"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartCommonOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" contains common host and presentation options.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" adds the definition. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPresentationOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" contains\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"class"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"style"},{"type":"text","value":". The package exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyDirective"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyTemplateContext"},{"type":"text","value":". It also\nre-exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"../adapter.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Angular adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for lifecycle and SSR behavior,\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Focus and interaction"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for\ncallback semantics, and "},{"type":"link","href":"../../../reference/rendering-and-export.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Rendering and export"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor custom SVG renderers."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"options","text":"options","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-template","text":"Tooltip body template","level":2},{"id":"exported-types","text":"Exported types","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/angular'\n```\n\n`Chart` is a standalone component with selector `tanstack-chart`. Its required\n`options` input accepts a chart definition. Replace the definition identity\nwhen captured application values change.\nThe definition also owns `focus`, `focusRing`, `cursor`, `tooltip`, `svgAnimation`,\n`keyboard`, `maxFocusDistance`, and `spatialIndex`.\n\n## `options`\n\n| Option               | Type                                         | Default               | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `definition`         | `ChartDefinition`                            | Required              | Framework-neutral chart definition                                  |\n| `ariaLabel`          | `string`                                     | Required              | Accessible chart name                                               |\n| `ariaDescription`    | `string`                                     | None                  | Optional accessible description                                     |\n| `height`             | `number`                                     | `320` without a ratio | Fixed CSS and scene height                                          |\n| `aspectRatio`        | `number`                                     | None                  | Positive width-to-height ratio when height is absent                |\n| `width`              | `number`                                     | Responsive            | Fixed CSS and scene width                                           |\n| `initialWidth`       | `number`                                     | `640`                 | Initial and server width before responsive measurement              |\n| `tabIndex`           | `number`                                     | `0`                   | Surface tab index; `keyboard: false` forces `-1`                    |\n| `idPrefix`           | `string`                                     | Generated             | Prefix for renderer-owned document IDs                              |\n| `renderSvg`          | `ChartSvgRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>` | `renderChartSvg`      | Scene-to-SVG renderer                                               |\n| `measureText`        | `ChartTextMeasurer`                          | Host measurer         | Guide text measurement                                              |\n| `onFocusChange`      | `(point: ChartPoint \\| null) => void`        | None                  | Primary focus callback                                              |\n| `onFocusGroupChange` | `(points: readonly ChartPoint[]) => void`    | None                  | Grouped focus callback                                              |\n| `onSelect`           | `(point: ChartPoint \\| null) => void`        | None                  | Pointer or keyboard activation callback                             |\n| `onRender`           | `(context: ChartRenderContext) => void`      | None                  | Default SVG, complete surface, container, and scene after rendering |\n| `class`              | `string`                                     | None                  | Extra class on the inner `.ts-chart-host`                           |\n| `style`              | `string`                                     | None                  | Inner host declarations applied after adapter sizing                |\n| `className`          | `string`                                     | None                  | Extra class on the rendered chart surface                           |\n\nCallbacks are functions inside `options`, not Angular outputs. Replace the\ncomplete `options` value when chart state changes so `OnPush` change detection\ndelivers an `ngOnChanges` update.\n\n## Tooltip body template\n\nProject a typed tooltip template into the chart:\n\n```html\n<tanstack-chart [options]=\"chartOptions\">\n  <ng-template [tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"chartOptions.definition\" let-tooltip>\n    <ng-container [ngTemplateOutlet]=\"tooltip.defaultBody\" />\n    <series-detail [points]=\"tooltip.points\" />\n    @if (tooltip.pinned) {\n    <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"tooltip.dismiss()\">Close</button>\n    }\n  </ng-template>\n</tanstack-chart>\n```\n\nImport `ChartTooltipBodyDirective` and Angular's `NgTemplateOutlet` beside\n`Chart`. The context exposes `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`, and\n`dismiss`; named template bindings are also available. Binding the same\ndefinition gives Angular's strict template checker the datum and x/y value\ntypes. Ordering, anchoring, placement, portaling, and pinning remain in the\ndefinition.\n\n## Exported types\n\n`ChartCommonOptions` contains common host and presentation options.\n`ChartOptions` adds the definition. `ChartPresentationOptions` contains\n`class` and `style`. The package exports `ChartTooltipBodyDirective`,\n`ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`, and `ChartTooltipBodyTemplateContext`. It also\nre-exports `ChartDefinition` and `ChartPoint`.\n\nSee the [Angular adapter](../adapter.md) for lifecycle and SSR behavior,\n[Focus and interaction](../../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md) for\ncallback semantics, and [Rendering and export](../../../reference/rendering-and-export.md)\nfor custom SVG renderers.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Angular Chart\ndescription: Complete option and type reference for the @tanstack/charts/angular standalone component.\n---\n\n```ts\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/angular'\n```\n\n`Chart` is a standalone component with selector `tanstack-chart`. Its required\n`options` input accepts a chart definition. Replace the definition identity\nwhen captured application values change.\nThe definition also owns `focus`, `focusRing`, `cursor`, `tooltip`, `svgAnimation`,\n`keyboard`, `maxFocusDistance`, and `spatialIndex`.\n\n## `options`\n\n| Option               | Type                                         | Default               | Meaning                                                             |\n| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `definition`         | `ChartDefinition`                            | Required              | Framework-neutral chart definition                                  |\n| `ariaLabel`          | `string`                                     | Required              | Accessible chart name                                               |\n| `ariaDescription`    | `string`                                     | None                  | Optional accessible description                                     |\n| `height`             | `number`                                     | `320` without a ratio | Fixed CSS and scene height                                          |\n| `aspectRatio`        | `number`                                     | None                  | Positive width-to-height ratio when height is absent                |\n| `width`              | `number`                                     | Responsive            | Fixed CSS and scene width                                           |\n| `initialWidth`       | `number`                                     | `640`                 | Initial and server width before responsive measurement              |\n| `tabIndex`           | `number`                                     | `0`                   | Surface tab index; `keyboard: false` forces `-1`                    |\n| `idPrefix`           | `string`                                     | Generated             | Prefix for renderer-owned document IDs                              |\n| `renderSvg`          | `ChartSvgRenderer<TDatum, TXValue, TYValue>` | `renderChartSvg`      | Scene-to-SVG renderer                                               |\n| `measureText`        | `ChartTextMeasurer`                          | Host measurer         | Guide text measurement                                              |\n| `onFocusChange`      | `(point: ChartPoint \\| null) => void`        | None                  | Primary focus callback                                              |\n| `onFocusGroupChange` | `(points: readonly ChartPoint[]) => void`    | None                  | Grouped focus callback                                              |\n| `onSelect`           | `(point: ChartPoint \\| null) => void`        | None                  | Pointer or keyboard activation callback                             |\n| `onRender`           | `(context: ChartRenderContext) => void`      | None                  | Default SVG, complete surface, container, and scene after rendering |\n| `class`              | `string`                                     | None                  | Extra class on the inner `.ts-chart-host`                           |\n| `style`              | `string`                                     | None                  | Inner host declarations applied after adapter sizing                |\n| `className`          | `string`                                     | None                  | Extra class on the rendered chart surface                           |\n\nCallbacks are functions inside `options`, not Angular outputs. Replace the\ncomplete `options` value when chart state changes so `OnPush` change detection\ndelivers an `ngOnChanges` update.\n\n## Tooltip body template\n\nProject a typed tooltip template into the chart:\n\n```html\n<tanstack-chart [options]=\"chartOptions\">\n  <ng-template [tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"chartOptions.definition\" let-tooltip>\n    <ng-container [ngTemplateOutlet]=\"tooltip.defaultBody\" />\n    <series-detail [points]=\"tooltip.points\" />\n    @if (tooltip.pinned) {\n    <button type=\"button\" (click)=\"tooltip.dismiss()\">Close</button>\n    }\n  </ng-template>\n</tanstack-chart>\n```\n\nImport `ChartTooltipBodyDirective` and Angular's `NgTemplateOutlet` beside\n`Chart`. The context exposes `points`, `content`, `defaultBody`, `pinned`, and\n`dismiss`; named template bindings are also available. Binding the same\ndefinition gives Angular's strict template checker the datum and x/y value\ntypes. Ordering, anchoring, placement, portaling, and pinning remain in the\ndefinition.\n\n## Exported types\n\n`ChartCommonOptions` contains common host and presentation options.\n`ChartOptions` adds the definition. `ChartPresentationOptions` contains\n`class` and `style`. The package exports `ChartTooltipBodyDirective`,\n`ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`, and `ChartTooltipBodyTemplateContext`. It also\nre-exports `ChartDefinition` and `ChartPoint`.\n\nSee the [Angular adapter](../adapter.md) for lifecycle and SSR behavior,\n[Focus and interaction](../../../reference/focus-and-interaction.md) for\ncallback semantics, and [Rendering and export](../../../reference/rendering-and-export.md)\nfor custom SVG renderers.\n"}
